{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:91b1079c3dd6f0c003bb20f34f3783141cbc55926e6e3001ba18eaba3acc169e", "sample_idx": 18, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "\"skill in solving Sudoku puzzles demands precision, much like navigating the complex weight of climate policy decisions. Each number placement mirrors the careful balance required when governments weigh temporary emissions cuts against long-term gas reduction goals — a twist of logic where every choice affects the whole system.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nThe grid’s constraints reflect the rigid frameworks imposed by international climate agreements: no repeats, no shortcuts, no exceptions. Just as a single misplaced digit can unravel an entire puzzle, a misjudged policy on gas infrastructure can derail decades of climate progress — making every decision carry immense weight.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nA temporary reprieve in regulatory pressure might seem like a welcome twist, but it risks undermining the integrity of the system. Climate scientists and puzzle masters alike know: shortcuts in one area create cascading failures elsewhere. The 3x3 boxes, like regional carbon budgets, must each hold their own balance without compromising the global whole.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nBuying next week’s Observer Digital Edition isn’t just about solving a puzzle — it’s about training the mind to see patterns in chaos. Whether it’s the weight of carbon emissions or the twist of political will, the same discipline applies: every row, every column, every box must hold truth — and truth, like a solved grid, demands patience, rigor, and integrity.\"", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -2.4437606043647975e-05}, {"token": "skill", "logprob": -0.0016066036187112331}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.02808956988155842}, {"token": " solving", "logprob": -0.015920665115118027}, {"token": " Sudoku", "logprob": -1.220703125}, {"token": " puzzles", "logprob": -0.170888289809227}, {"token": " demands", "logprob": -1.426460